WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.000
How can authors judge a translation
when they don't speak the language?

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:09.000
This is a very important step,
and this is why we introduced the human proofreader.

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:17.000
We have professional translators who work for us
in all of the different European languages.

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:25.000
They read excerpts from the book—around 5,000
to 8,000 words from different sections.

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:32.000
We choose the beginning, the end and a difficult-
to-translate part in the middle.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:37.000
When you get your book back, you can be confident
that it has been translated correctly.

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:48.000
Any feedback from the human translator is put back
into the manuscript, and it is checked one more time.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:54.000
When you get the scores back,
everything is marked out of five.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:01:00.000
Only anything that is a four or a five passes,
so you can have confidence in the book.
